{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.FrobeniusRelation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.FrobeniusRelation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.frobenius_relation_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.frobenius_relation_left","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-relation.lean#L44-L53","doc":"The Frobenius relation in \"left\" form:\n`(Δ ▷ A) ≫ α ≫ (A ◁ μ) = μ ≫ Δ`.\n\nThis is the direct field from `FrobeniusHopfData`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.frobenius_relation_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.frobenius_relation_holds","kind":"theorem","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-relation.lean#L23-L42","doc":"**Frobenius relation** (categorical form).\n\nFor a Frobenius–Hopf object `(A, μ, Δ)` in a monoidal category,\nthe Frobenius relation states that the two morphisms\n`A ⊗ A → A ⊗ A` obtained by:\n\n(1) `(id ⊗ Δ) ≫ (α⁻¹) ≫ (μ ⊗ id)`, and\n(2) `μ ≫ Δ`\n\nare equal.  This is already part of the `FrobeniusHopfData` axioms\n(`frobenius_relation` field).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:frobenius-relation}`\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","signatureChunk":0}]}